# FLY-519 — second line of defence for the ZERO-SECRET contract of fleet/.
# fleet-capture.sh already (1) redacts .env to key names and (2) runs
# scan_for_secrets as a hard gate before writing. This .gitignore makes it
# impossible to accidentally commit a real secret file even if those fail.
#
# The ONLY files meant to live here are: projects.json (env NAMES only),
# env.example (key names, zero values), manifest.json, and example/.

# Never commit a real env file or any of its backups.
.env
*.env
!env.example
!example/env.example

# Never commit databases (teamlead/audit/cipher/dedup) or auth material.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
codex-homes/
**/auth.json
**/*token*.json
**/*secret*

# Never commit raw backups that might carry values.
*.bak
*.backup
